ßbidx-urn:uuid:382b2244-5fd9-43f1-b680-ae934f0a7a47dtypeeOffereactorx"urn:ame:inference-work-lot-servicefobjectßdfuel@dtermÉdpairÇfeffect¨clawx9ni:///sha-256;h2VIEZwYH__6vRnSgSWYRrFh1AHFcIBFboED8rlsGgoescaledtaskfcallerx7eip155:31337:0xd04d2227a96c0a318ee6047380fd78543fa2683afparentˆgoutcome¢pnegativeEvidenceÙppositiveEvidenceÙgrefusalx9ni:///sha-256;dKkVbwsRhSztfcXc8s6bEA1zB0AaTOYCeq2YaMXRx1ohmeasuresÅ£dunitnprovider-offerhquantityb35idimensionx"relative-resolution-milliquanta-v1hproviderx7eip155:31337:0xf5aa437b826d3b035300e1423942a2a4f575ba9dioperationx9ni:///sha-256;OyhyVcTS7UKx1G9WguvRLGJ3ItTOSte8K5zW1YN8oM4levidenceRootx9ni:///sha-256;krjMOYWwQ4I6gAWpSyE_Ha09eUxK8AsmcWeW1qjtEtklpreconditionx9ni:///sha-256;dNesJQyez0bdbcpTM1MtfCR7L9ar5uIlOkLx60zfHHYmpostconditionx9ni:///sha-256;0jnKWsRluPhZTSFnptsDbKtZmi11UxWwELinxoxKrugÉdpairÇdmarkyReturn one candidate derivation for the supplied typed unresolved residue. Do not claim customer acceptance, execution, or truth. Output only one JSON value: no Markdown fence, comments, or prose. The exact customer schema is {"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["list_files","search","read","edit","command","test","finish"],"type":"string"},"args":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"reason":{"maxLength":500,"minLength":5,"type":"string"}},"required":["action","args","reason"],"type":"object"}.ÉdpairÇdmarky©:{"context":{"messages":[{"content":"You are an autonomous software worker operating an isolated copy of one admitted territory. Invoke exactly one tool per response using the contracted JSON. Available actions:\nlist_files {path?,max?}; search {query,path?}; read {path,startLine?,endLine?}; edit {path,blocks}; command {name}; test {}; finish {summary?}.\nInclude only the arguments used by the selected action. For edit, blocks must be objects shaped {search,replace}; do not put marker text inside either field. To create a new file use exactly one block with search:\"\" and replace containing the whole new file. A read observation's text field contains exact unnumbered source bytes; copy from it byte-for-byte into an existing-file search block. You have no shell. Inspect declared focus paths first, then edit as soon as enough evidence is available. Do not explore operational data records unless the objective names them. Make the smallest correct change. The host automatically runs the declared verification after every edit. Never claim success without a passing verification result.","role":"system"},{"content":"CODING CONTEXT PACKET (host-compiled; artifact text is exact and unnumbered unless marked truncated):\n\n{\"type\":\"AutonomousCodingContextPacket\",\"id\":\"urn:ame:free-compute-dev:mission:2026-07-19-retire-liss-broker-readme:context\",\"identity\":{\"missionId\":\"urn:ame:free-compute-dev:mission:2026-07-19-retire-liss-broker-readme\",\"taskClass\":\"documentation-carrier-rectification\",\"actorRole\":\"bounded software worker\",\"hostRole\":\"scope enforcement, evidence assembly, execution, verification, semantic review, and protected-border integration\"},\"objective\":\"Repair README.md so its operating description matches the live typed customer-side procurement circuit. Remove claims that a persistent LISS broker, filesystem spool, socket, dispatcher, or LISS-owned provider selection is the default. Explain that free-compute-dev emits a context-complete TypedRmnInferenceDemand; provider settlements author comparable offers; inference-work-lot-service selects the cheapest capable offer; LISS carries only the exact selected nested RMN contract through A2A; and free-compute-dev independently schema-assays the candidate before bounded tool execution. Preserve the historical Live result as history but clearly distinguish the retired carrier from the current mechanism.\",\"machineChecks\":{\"verifyCommand\":\"npm test\",\"acceptanceCommand\":\"node -e \\\"const s=require('fs').readFileSync('README.md','utf8');process.exit(s.includes('selection remains LISS-owned')||s.includes('persistent LISS broker accepts')||!s.includes('TypedRmnInferenceDemand')||!s.includes('typed-customer-procurement'))\\\"\",\"baselineVerification\":{\"passed\":true,\"output\":\"exit=0\"},\"baselineAcceptance\":{\"passed\":false,\"output\":\"exit=1\\n\\nnode:internal/errors:542\\n      throw error;\\n      ^\\n\\nTypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]: The \\\"code\\\" argument must be of type number. Received type boolean (true)\\n    at process.set [as exitCode] (node:internal/bootstrap/node:119:9)\\n    at process.exit (node:internal/process/per_thread:231:24)\\n    at [eval]:1:64\\n    at runScriptInThisContext (node:internal/vm:219:10)\\n    at node:internal/process/execution:451:12\\n    at [eval]-wrapper:6:24\\n    at runScriptInContext (node:internal/process/execution:449:60)\\n    at evalFunction (node:internal/process/execution:283:30)\\n    at evalTypeScript (node:internal/process/execution:295:3)\\n    at node:internal/main/eval_string:71:3 {\\n  code: 'ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE'\\n}\\n\\nNode.js v24.13.1\\n\\n\"}},\"acceptanceTestVectors\":[{\"id\":\"typed-customer-procurement\",\"given\":[\"a context-complete coding work residue\",\"finite sovereign supplier offers\"],\"when\":\"free-compute-dev needs one inference act\",\"then\":[\"customer-side selection occurs before LISS invocation\",\"the selected exact RMN contract crosses A2A\",\"free-compute-dev independently assays the result\"],\"forbidden\":[\"LISS-owned selection\",\"filesystem spool as the active carrier\",\"provider self-attestation as acceptance\"]}],\"acceptanceTraceability\":{\"rule\":\"Every acceptanceTestVector id must occur verbatim in a changed artifact before the host may recognize a verification-passing candidate.\",\"requiredMarkers\":[\"typed-customer-procurement\"]},\"acceptanceAuthority\":{\"protected\":false,\"mode\":\"candidate-writable-or-unresolved\",\"commandTargets\":[\"README.md\"],\"capsuleId\":null,\"capsuleDigest\":null,\"rule\":\"A trajectory is promotable only when every explicit acceptance-command artifact pre-exists and is outside the candidate writable lane.\"},\"lane\":{\"territory\":\"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/free-compute-dev\",\"focusPaths\":[\"README.md\",\"src/fabric-client.mjs\",\"content/contracts/typed-inference-procurement.rml\"],\"writablePaths\":[\"README.md\"],\"readablePaths\":[\"README.md\",\"src/fabric-client.mjs\",\"content/contracts/typed-inference-procurement.rml\",\"package.json\"],\"protectedOrExcluded\":[\"paths outside territory\",\"undeclared writable paths when writablePaths is nonempty\",\".git\",\"node_modules\",\".lake\",\"dist\",\"coverage\",\"operational data records unless the objective names them\"]},\"targetArtifacts\":[],\"evidenceArtifacts\":[{\"path\":\"content/contracts/typed-inference-procurement.rml\",\"role\":\"focus\",\"digest\":\"sha256:4a938c0994b521133836f20e22e82f23f60412eeb761db035782253d2a4ed2a2\",\"bytes\":244,\"truncated\":false,\"text\":\"#lang rmn/v2\\n(predicate \\\"free-compute-dev-typed-inference-procurement-v1\\\"\\n  (base \\\"ContextCompleteSoftwareWorkDemand\\\")\\n  (base \\\"ProviderAuthoredComparableOffer\\\")\\n  (base \\\"WitnessedRmnInferenceCandidate\\\")\\n  (base \\\"FreeComputeDevCustomerAssay\\\"))\\n\"},{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"role\":\"focus\",\"digest\":\"sha256:967ff83af29997aa090e269f9bed500c3a7bd8030557b2e93c932aac9181f00a\",\"bytes\":6170,\"truncated\":false,\"text\":\"# free-compute-dev\\n\\nAn autonomous software-development harness built on the firm's stated economics:\\n\\n- **Default effort = contributed compute.** Patch generation and iteration run on\\n  the cheapest sufficient endpoint currently admitted by LISS (today Groq, Gemini,\\n  GitHub Models, OpenRouter when available, and later private GPU workers).\\n- **`claude -p` is the gated exception**, not the default ‚Äî used as a quality gate and\\n  for problems above a difficulty threshold, because it is the expensive resource.\\n\\nThis is a persistent software-production fabric, not a conversational coding\\nwrapper. A caller can submit an objective and leave. The fabric observes the\\nterritory, contracts parallel inference, executes bounded tools, verifies\\ncandidates, integrates one without overwriting concurrent work, and records the\\nsuccessful trajectory for reuse.\\n\\n## Live result\\n\\nOn 2026-07-19, three isolated workers contracted Groq, Gemini, and GitHub Models\\nthrough the persistent LISS broker. They made 17 useful tool decisions over eight\\nwaves. Gemini independently navigated to `src/executor.mjs`, derived a two-edit\\nrepair for a real temporary-directory leak, passed the package suite in\\nisolation, and the runtime atomically integrated and reverified it. No interactive\\nmodel call supplied the patch. The first run also taught the deterministic carrier\\nto accept providers' native JSON action dialects and structured `{search,replace}`\\nedit arrays.\\n\\nThe next unattended queued mission exposed a task-class capability boundary: three\\ncheap actors could not author a semantically valid early-quorum regression. The\\nbounded residue was resubmitted through the queue to Claude with provider-enforced\\nJSON Schema. Claude inspected the test and runtime, authored the regression, and\\nthe queue integrated it after verification. The resulting 26-test suite proves\\nearly quorum, dead-worker claim abandonment, protected-border integration, and the\\ndurable carrier itself. The failed cheap trajectory remains evidence for future\\ntask-class pricing instead of being hidden.\\n\\n## Operating surfaces\\n\\n- `run-union-dev-mission mission.json` runs one objective through parallel isolated\\n  tool workers and a verification/integration gate.\\n- `run-union-dev-program program.json` asks multiple cloud planners for acyclic\\n  mission DAGs, validates them, and executes the cheapest valid plan until the\\n  declared program acceptance command passes.\\n- `submit-union-dev-mission mission.json` and `run-union-dev-worker` provide a\\n  durable queue, claims, heartbeats, stale-claim recovery, and unattended service.\\n- `abandon-union-dev-mission exact-id reason` terminally settles work whose worker\\n  was deliberately stopped, preventing stale recovery from purchasing obsolete\\n  inference again.\\n- LISS's persistent broker accepts batches through a filesystem spool as well as a\\n  Unix socket. Sandboxed workers need neither network access nor provider keys;\\n  they atomically signal jobs through the spool while the one broker owns cloud\\n  access, pricing, concurrency, replay, and the append-only settlement journal.\\n\\nEach worker can `list_files`, `search`, `read`, apply exact edits, run the declared\\nverification/acceptance gates, and invoke only commands pre-admitted by the mission.\\nCandidate workspaces are copies; integration compares source digests and classifies\\na concurrent source change as a protected border instead of overwriting it.\\n\\nAn unresolved base phase is automatically re-contracted as `software-engineering`\\nwork requiring schema-validated actions. LISS then quotes only suppliers with that\\ncapability instead of repeatedly buying cheap syntactic completions. Successful\\nbase‚Üíescalation routes are appended by task class; a later mission of that class\\nstarts at the witnessed sufficient stage unless its manifest explicitly refuses\\nlearned routing. Program-DAG missions use the same pipeline.\\n\\nExecution-passing candidates are not integrated on that evidence alone. Unless a\\nmission explicitly declines semantic review, three independently sharded cloud\\nreviewers compare the changed source to the original objective and constraints.\\nA valid-review majority is required. Rejected candidates remain isolated, and the\\nreview reasons become residue for a second software-engineering revision stage.\\nDeclared writable paths are enforced by the tool carrier rather than trusted to a\\nprompt.\\n\\n## The solve loop ([src/solve-loop.mjs](src/solve-loop.mjs))\\n\\nMAPE-K over a working tree:\\n\\n1. **Route** ‚Äî if an upfront difficulty estimate is at/above the threshold, skip free\\n   rounds and escalate straight to `claude -p` (don't waste rounds on research-hard work).\\n2. **Generate ‚Üí Apply ‚Üí Test** ‚Äî up to `maxFreeRounds` on free inference; each failed\\n   round feeds its test output back as context (this is the Analyze‚ÜíPlan feedback).\\n3. **Escalate** ‚Äî if free rounds are exhausted without passing tests, escalate to\\n   `claude -p`, then re-run tests to confirm.\\n4. Return `solved-free | solved-escalated | failed` with a full round log.\\n\\nEvery dependency (`generatePatch`, `applyPatch`, `runTests`, `escalate`, `difficulty`) is\\ninjectable, so the escalation *policy* is tested deterministically with mocks\\n([test/solve-loop.test.mjs](test/solve-loop.test.mjs)) without spending real inference.\\n\\n## Recursive improvement\\n\\nEvery run appends its tool/result trajectory. Later missions recall similar verified\\nactions. Structural action fingerprints accumulate by task class; after repeated\\nhigh-verification recurrence, the promotion readout marks the class eligible to become\\na deterministic resolver. Provider dialect failures are rectified in the carrier, so a\\nnew cycle inherits what prior cycles learned rather than requiring another prompt.\\n\\n## Default implementations\\n\\n- Inference: [src/fabric-client.mjs](src/fabric-client.mjs) ‚Äî batches work through the\\n  LISS spool/socket/dispatcher boundary; provider selection remains LISS-owned.\\n- Executor: [src/executor.mjs](src/executor.mjs) ‚Äî `git apply` a unified diff, run a test\\n  command, capture exit/stdout/stderr.\\n- Escalation: [src/escalate.mjs](src/escalate.mjs) ‚Äî spawn `claude -p` in the work tree.\\n\"},{\"path\":\"src/fabric-client.mjs\",\"role\":\"focus\",\"digest\":\"sha256:b6517d006c18f9326f1e9f759e8c9e79413db525ed3efd46ddd1bff092f72c71\",\"bytes\":8779,\"truncated\":false,\"text\":\"import { spawn } from \\\"node:child_process\\\";\\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport { dirname, resolve } from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\nimport { procureTypedInference } from \\\"@emsenn/inference-work-lot-service/typed-rmn-inference-procurement\\\";\\nimport { assayTypedInferenceCandidate } from \\\"@emsenn/inference-work-lot-service/customer-assay-typed-inference\\\";\\n\\nconst HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst ROOT = resolve(HERE, \\\"..\\\");\\nconst WORKSPACE = resolve(ROOT, \\\"../../../../../..\\\");\\nconst LISS = resolve(WORKSPACE, \\\"lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/red-cup-engineering/services/logical-inference-service-section\\\");\\nconst LISS_EXECUTOR = resolve(LISS, \\\"src/contract-rmn-inference.mjs\\\");\\nconst NPU = resolve(LISS, \\\"services/bare-cedar-fog-npu-inference-team\\\");\\nconst GEMINI = resolve(LISS, \\\"services/gemini-inference-team\\\");\\nconst ACCOUNT_BINDING = resolve(ROOT, \\\"content/evm/accounts/eip155-31337.json\\\");\\nconst ACTOR = \\\"urn:ame:free-compute-dev\\\";\\n\\nconst PROVIDERS = Object.freeze([\\n  Object.freeze({\\n    id: \\\"bare-cedar-fog-npu-qwen3.5-0.8b-flm\\\",\\n    actor: \\\"urn:ame:bare-cedar-fog-npu-inference-team\\\",\\n    solicitation: resolve(NPU, \\\"src/solicit-rmn-inference.mjs\\\"),\\n    cwd: NPU,\\n    agentCard: () => process.env.UNION_NPU_AGENT_CARD_URL ?? \\\"http://127.0.0.1:17771/.well-known/agent-card.json\\\",\\n  }),\\n  Object.freeze({\\n    id: \\\"gemini-3.1-flash-lite\\\",\\n    actor: \\\"urn:ame:gemini-inference-team\\\",\\n    solicitation: resolve(GEMINI, \\\"src/solicit-rmn-inference.mjs\\\"),\\n    cwd: GEMINI,\\n    agentCard: () => process.env.UNION_GEMINI_AGENT_CARD_URL ?? \\\"http://127.0.0.1:17772/.well-known/agent-card.json\\\",\\n  }),\\n]);\\n\\nfunction aborted(reason = \\\"inference procurement aborted\\\") {\\n  const error = new Error(typeof reason === \\\"string\\\" ? reason : \\\"inference procurement aborted\\\");\\n  error.name = \\\"AbortError\\\";\\n  return error;\\n}\\n\\nfunction run(command, args, { cwd, input, env = process.env, timeoutMs = 1_200_000, signal } = {}) {\\n  return new Promise((accept, reject) => {\\n    if (signal?.aborted) { reject(aborted(signal.reason)); return; }\\n    const child = spawn(command, args, { cwd, env, stdio: [\\\"pipe\\\", \\\"pipe\\\", \\\"pipe\\\"] });\\n    let stdout = \\\"\\\", stderr = \\\"\\\", settled = false;\\n    const finish = (error, value) => {\\n      if (settled) return;\\n      settled = true; clearTimeout(timer); signal?.removeEventListener(\\\"abort\\\", stop);\\n      if (error) reject(error); else accept(value);\\n    };\\n    const stop = () => { child.kill(\\\"SIGTERM\\\"); finish(aborted(signal.reason)); };\\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => { child.kill(\\\"SIGKILL\\\"); finish(new Error(`contracted process exceeded ${timeoutMs}ms`)); }, timeoutMs);\\n    signal?.addEventListener(\\\"abort\\\", stop, { once: true });\\n    child.stdout.on(\\\"data\\\", (chunk) => { stdout += chunk; });\\n    child.stderr.on(\\\"data\\\", (chunk) => { stderr += chunk; });\\n    child.on(\\\"error\\\", (error) => finish(error));\\n    child.on(\\\"close\\\", (code, childSignal) => code === 0\\n      ? finish(undefined, { stdout, stderr })\\n      : finish(new Error(`contracted process refused with code ${code ?? \\\"none\\\"}${childSignal ? ` signal ${childSignal}` : \\\"\\\"}: ${stderr.slice(0, 1200)}`)));\\n    child.stdin.end(input ?? \\\"\\\");\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction suppliersFor(job, signal) {\\n  const preferred = Array.isArray(job.preferEndpoints) ? job.preferEndpoints : [];\\n  const providers = preferred.length\\n    ? PROVIDERS.filter((provider) => preferred.includes(provider.id) || preferred.includes(provider.actor))\\n    : PROVIDERS;\\n  return providers.map((provider) => ({\\n    actor: provider.actor,\\n    endpoint: provider.id,\\n    agentCard: provider.agentCard(),\\n    async exchange(activity) {\\n      const result = await run(process.execPath, [provider.solicitation], { cwd: provider.cwd, input: `${JSON.stringify(activity)}\\\\n`, timeoutMs: 30_000, signal });\\n      return JSON.parse(result.stdout);\\n    },\\n  }));\\n}\\n\\nfunction customer() {\\n  if (!existsSync(ACCOUNT_BINDING)) throw new Error(\\\"free-compute-dev has no sovereign EVM account binding\\\");\\n  const binding = JSON.parse(readFileSync(ACCOUNT_BINDING, \\\"utf8\\\"));\\n  return { actor: ACTOR, account: binding.account?.caip10 };\\n}\\n\\nfunction requestFor(job, suppliers) {\\n  const schema = job.outputContract?.schema ?? {};\\n  return {\\n    workLot: { id: job.id, producer: ACTOR },\\n    context: {\\n      messages: job.messages,\\n      purpose: \\\"Produce one candidate for independent free-compute-dev assay and bounded tool execution.\\\",\\n      providerPreference: job.preferEndpoints ?? [],\\n    },\\n    actuatorTerms: {\\n      workType: job.workType ?? \\\"inquiry\\\",\\n      requiredCapabilities: job.requiredCapabilities ?? [\\\"inquiry\\\", \\\"json-output\\\"],\\n      difficulty: Number.isFinite(job.difficulty) ? job.difficulty : 0.5,\\n      maxTokens: Number.isInteger(job.maxTokens) ? job.maxTokens : 2048,\\n      mode: job.mode ?? \\\"live\\\",\\n      outputContract: { ...(job.outputContract ?? { format: \\\"json\\\" }), schema },\\n      agentCards: suppliers.map(({ actor, agentCard }) => ({ actor, url: agentCard })),\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction candidateText(procurement) {\\n  return procurement?.settlement?.object?.attachment?.find(({ type, mediaType }) => type === \\\"Note\\\" && mediaType === \\\"text/plain\\\")?.content ?? \\\"\\\";\\n}\\n\\nasync function procureJob(job, { timeoutMs, signal, env, procure = procureTypedInference } = {}) {\\n  if (signal?.aborted) throw aborted(signal.reason);\\n  const started = Date.now();\\n  const suppliers = suppliersFor(job, signal);\\n  if (suppliers.length === 0) return { id: job.id, attempts: [], refusal: { type: \\\"preferred-provider-not-admitted\\\", reason: \\\"no named preferred endpoint is an admitted typed supplier\\\" }, latencyMs: Date.now() - started };\\n  const request = requestFor(job, suppliers);\\n  const residue = { type: \\\"TypedWorkInferenceResidue\\\", workLot: job.id, reason: \\\"no deterministic resolver covered the next context-complete work move\\\", customerAcceptanceRequired: true };\\n  const liss = { async invoke(source) {\\n    const carried = await run(process.execPath, [LISS_EXECUTOR], { cwd: LISS, input: `${JSON.stringify(source)}\\\\n`, env, timeoutMs: timeoutMs ?? 1_200_000, signal });\\n    return JSON.parse(carried.stdout);\\n  } };\\n  const procurement = await procure({ residue, request, suppliers, caller: customer(), liss });\\n  const selected = procurement.selection?.selected;\\n  const endpoint = suppliers.find(({ actor }) => actor === selected?.provider?.actor)?.endpoint ?? selected?.provider?.actor ?? null;\\n  const latencyMs = Date.now() - started;\\n  if (procurement.disposition !== \\\"candidate-pending-customer-assay\\\") {\\n    return { id: job.id, endpoint, attempts: endpoint ? [{ endpoint, outcome: \\\"refusal\\\", reason: procurement.disposition, latencyMs }] : [], refusal: { type: procurement.disposition, market: procurement.market?.refused ?? [] }, latencyMs, procurement: { frontierInferenceCalls: procurement.frontierInferenceCalls } };\\n  }\\n  const assay = assayTypedInferenceCandidate(procurement, { customer: ACTOR, dataRoot: resolve(ROOT, \\\"data\\\") });\\n  if (!assay.accepted) return { id: job.id, endpoint, attempts: [{ endpoint, outcome: \\\"customer-refusal\\\", reason: assay.problems.join(\\\"; \\\"), latencyMs }], refusal: { type: \\\"customer-assay-refused\\\", problems: assay.problems }, latencyMs, assay };\\n  return {\\n    id: job.id,\\n    endpoint,\\n    model: selected.offer.object.model,\\n    attempts: [{ endpoint, outcome: \\\"completion\\\", expectedResolutionCost: selected.offer.object.consideration.amount, unit: selected.offer.object.consideration.unit, latencyMs }],\\n    text: candidateText(procurement),\\n    usage: null,\\n    cost: selected.offer.object.consideration,\\n    verification: { customerAssay: assay.id, accepted: true, providerSelfAttestation: false },\\n    latencyMs,\\n    settlement: procurement.settlement.object.completion,\\n    procurement: { outerProposal: procurement.contract.outer.term, childProposal: procurement.contract.child.term, frontierInferenceCalls: procurement.frontierInferenceCalls },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function dispatchBatch(jobs, options = {}) {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(jobs) || jobs.length === 0) return [];\\n  if (options.signal?.aborted) throw aborted(options.signal.reason);\\n  const concurrency = Math.max(1, Math.min(Number(options.concurrency) || 8, 64));\\n  const records = new Array(jobs.length);\\n  let next = 0;\\n  const workers = Array.from({ length: Math.min(concurrency, jobs.length) }, async () => {\\n    while (next < jobs.length) {\\n      const index = next; next += 1;\\n      records[index] = await procureJob(jobs[index], options);\\n    }\\n  });\\n  await Promise.all(workers);\\n  return records;\\n}\\n\\nexport const fabricDefaults = Object.freeze({ customer: ACTOR, providers: PROVIDERS.map(({ id, actor }) => ({ id, actor })), selectionOwner: \\\"urn:ame:inference-work-lot-service\\\", carrier: [\\\"ActivityStreams\\\", \\\"RMN\\\", \\\"A2A 1.0\\\"] });\\n\"},{\"path\":\"package.json\",\"role\":\"package-manifest\",\"digest\":\"sha256:1b226a8eec3b4f3df99a60c50c1da1a03eb0deda09d36ed09e4a7d328f816bc5\",\"bytes\":1782,\"truncated\":false,\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"@emsenn/free-compute-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.1\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Persistent autonomous software-production fabric: cloud-planned mission DAGs, parallel isolated tool-using workers, verified integration, durable queues, trajectory memory, and resolver-promotion evidence through LISS.\\\",\\n  \\\"bin\\\": {\\n    \\\"run-union-dev-mission\\\": \\\"bin/run-mission.mjs\\\",\\n    \\\"run-union-dev-program\\\": \\\"bin/run-program.mjs\\\",\\n    \\\"submit-union-dev-mission\\\": \\\"bin/submit-mission.mjs\\\",\\n    \\\"run-union-dev-worker\\\": \\\"bin/run-worker.mjs\\\",\\n    \\\"abandon-union-dev-mission\\\": \\\"bin/abandon-mission.mjs\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"node --test\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@emsenn/inference-work-lot-service\\\": \\\"file:../../../board-of-directors/services/executive-office/services/working-services-section/services/inference-work-lot-service\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"x-agentic-metro-enterprise\\\": {\\n    \\\"node-id\\\": \\\"free-compute-dev\\\",\\n    \\\"owners\\\": [\\\"561-group\\\"],\\n    \\\"membrane\\\": {\\\"law\\\": \\\"lib/\\\", \\\"lasting-instances\\\": \\\"content/\\\", \\\"append-only-instances\\\": \\\"data/\\\"},\\n    \\\"admission\\\": \\\"one bounded software-production mission with exact territory, writable lane, context packet, and customer acceptance command\\\",\\n    \\\"refusal\\\": \\\"unbounded tools, incomplete software-engineering context, provider self-attestation, customer-border overwrite, or inference without a typed procurement settlement\\\",\\n    \\\"inference-procurement\\\": {\\n      \\\"provider\\\": \\\"urn:ame:inference-work-lot-service\\\",\\n      \\\"contract\\\": \\\"content/contracts/typed-inference-procurement.rml\\\",\\n      \\\"carrier\\\": [\\\"ActivityStreams\\\", \\\"RMN\\\", \\\"A2A 1.0\\\"],\\n      \\\"selectionOwner\\\": \\\"customer-side inference-work-lot-service\\\",\\n      \\\"acceptanceOwner\\\": \\\"urn:ame:free-compute-dev\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"LicenseRef-561Group-1.0\\\"\\n}\\n\"}],\"omittedArtifacts\":[],\"repositoryMap\":{\"filesObser